The historical check found a substantive residue, not just wording: the Network Objects DGC paper describes reference listing with dirty/clean calls and process-failure detection, but contains no lease/expiration mechanism. RMI combines that lineage with expiring leases; the current straight arrow “Gray & Cheriton → Network Objects → RMI → Jini” is therefore too strong. I’m consolidating this with the normative findings now.
